# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  hornflow - what is source, and what is generated
#
#  Rule: anything the pipeline or the test suite *produces* is ignored; anything
#  a human wrote, or that a test *needs to read*, is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- generated run artifacts (never source) --------------------------------
runs/
results/

# --- test / tooling caches --------------------------------------------------
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- third-party solver distribution (do NOT commit) ------------------------
# AKABAK Free 3.3.2 b144 (~426 MB of Windows binaries, zips and help files) is
# unpacked into AKABAK/ for the manual GUI solve.  It is third-party software
# redistributed by RDTeam, not part of this project, and far too large for git.
# Keep it on disk; the pipeline only needs its path (params/environment.akabak_exe).
# See history.md section 0 and docs/migration-notes.md.
AKABAK/

# --- editor / OS noise ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- local scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
*.log
tmp/
scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Tracked on purpose (do not add to the list above)
#  * tests/fixtures/bem_export/*.vips  - real AKABAK exports used by the golden
#    .vips parser tests.  Copied out of results/ precisely so results/ can stay
#    generated.
#  * tests/fixtures/baseline/          - frozen JBL numbers + curves.csv whose
#    sha256 is asserted, so it must stay byte-identical.
#  * hornflow/viz/viewer/vendor/       - vendored three.js r128 (MIT), needed for
#    the offline viewer (ADR-0009).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
